Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Storm-Flags Chew the Jetty
- Story & Context: When a Saharan salt-truck convoy broke its axle outside the Nouadhibou slipway in October 1977, driver Ibrahim unloaded a solder-scorched Farfisa organ onto the rain-drenched dock in exchange for three drums of marine diesel, where Kofi Annan immediately plugged it into an overdriven Selmer amplifier inside the customs shed. The sudden, deafening shriek of desert-fried electronics over furious 150-BPM congas triggered a flash riot between striking stevedores and French naval police as the smell of burning copper wire mingled with diesel exhaust. Standing atop a mountain of damp groundnut sacks while batons cracked against the zinc walls, Kofi spat into the salt wind and screamed, "The harbor eats our brothers while the rich men count the knots!" birthing the band's frantic, mournful war-cry.
