Track 2: “Who Cut the Mooring Hawser?”
- Story & Context: Written during a sleepless night inside a grounded tugboat cabin reeking of battery acid and stale tobacco, this confessional track captures Kofi’s anguish after his younger brother vanished aboard an unlicensed Mauritanian phosphate freighter bound for Las Palmas. During the live-to-tape session at a local radio transmitter room, Ibrahim teased an eerie, detuned whistle from a salvaged monophonic synth while the Diop brothers bruised their palms bloody against waterlogged conga skins, pushing the tempo until Kofi broke down mid-take into an unvarnished sob. The raw take was preserved without overdubs, immortalizing his ragged, overdriven falsetto hook: "You cut the hemp and let him drift into the black water, so do not look me in the eye when the tide turns back."
